1
00:01:33,560 --> 00:01:35,360
-<i>I'm going to Poipet.</i>
-<i>Huh?</i>

2
00:01:35,440 --> 00:01:36,960
<i>You're going to Poipet right now?</i>

3
00:01:37,040 --> 00:01:38,880
<i>Sis Hong, have you seen Risa?</i>

4
00:01:38,960 --> 00:01:39,880
<i>I saw her briefly this morning.</i>

5
00:01:39,960 --> 00:01:41,520
Ris asked me to look up information

6
00:01:41,600 --> 00:01:44,120
<i>about Hyena Group in Poipet.</i>

7
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:46,560
<i>Wait. Is this about Koh going to Cambodia?</i>

8
00:01:46,640 --> 00:01:49,240
What do you know? Tell me everything now.

9
00:01:49,320 --> 00:01:53,000
<i>No one here is allowed</i>
<i>to contact outsiders.</i>

10
00:01:53,080 --> 00:01:55,080
<i>Everyone gets a salary of 25,000.</i>

11
00:01:55,160 --> 00:01:56,440
So what's the job?

12
00:01:56,520 --> 00:01:59,600
Risa's my dear friend. If you expect me
to just stand by, I can't.

13
00:01:59,680 --> 00:02:02,960
If I knew this was a scam call center,
I never would've applied.

14
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:05,000
Crying won't change anything.

15
00:02:05,080 --> 00:02:07,000
Do you know someone named Louis?

16
00:02:07,080 --> 00:02:09,039
Anyone who messes with Louis
doesn't make it out.

17
00:02:09,120 --> 00:02:12,200
If they figure out who we're looking for,
what do you think they'll do to Risa?

18
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:17,440
Where's your phone?

19
00:02:19,360 --> 00:02:20,200
What phone?

20
00:02:21,160 --> 00:02:24,640
The phone you snuck into the bathroom
to make calls. Hand it over now.

21
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:28,040
What are you talking about?
I have no idea.

22
00:02:28,120 --> 00:02:30,440
Someone reported
that you smuggled a phone out.

23
00:02:30,520 --> 00:02:33,600
Hand it over, or the guards will deal
with you the same way they did last time.

24
00:02:35,480 --> 00:02:36,320
Now.

25
00:02:43,040 --> 00:02:43,880
Move.

26
00:02:45,440 --> 00:02:46,320
Search her.

27
00:02:48,920 --> 00:02:49,840
Stand up.

28
00:02:54,080 --> 00:02:56,840
Just because you hit your targets
doesn't mean you can do whatever you want.

29
00:02:57,440 --> 00:02:59,120
If I find that phone,

30
00:02:59,200 --> 00:03:01,480
you'll be locked up for good.

31
00:03:03,200 --> 00:03:04,280
Nothing, sir.

32
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:05,560
Search everything thoroughly.

33
00:03:06,960 --> 00:03:08,840
I wouldn't do something that stupid.

34
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:17,040
Find anything?

35
00:03:20,960 --> 00:03:21,920
Nothing, sir.

36
00:03:23,800 --> 00:03:26,880
But I saw it with my own eyes.
She took the phone out.

37
00:03:31,680 --> 00:03:32,520
Search her.

38
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:03,080
Nothing, sir.

39
00:04:05,880 --> 00:04:07,280
Are you lying to me?

40
00:04:07,360 --> 00:04:09,440
I really saw it. I'm not lying.

41
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:11,200
-Come over here.
-No!

42
00:04:11,280 --> 00:04:12,680
I'm telling the truth.
Please don't do anything to me.

43
00:04:12,760 --> 00:04:14,200
-I swear I'm telling the truth!
-Come here.

44
00:04:14,280 --> 00:04:16,880
-Don't kill me. I don't want to die.
-Hey!

45
00:04:17,800 --> 00:04:18,839
-Sir!
-Come here.

46
00:04:20,399 --> 00:04:21,600
That was close.

47
00:04:25,040 --> 00:04:28,120
So, where did you hide my phone?

48
00:05:01,960 --> 00:05:05,480
Hey, how much longer? I'm getting tired.
There are so many mosquitoes.

49
00:05:05,560 --> 00:05:07,560
Why are you standing there? Sit down.

50
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:10,320
Stop striking poses.

51
00:05:10,400 --> 00:05:13,560
My outfit looks good. The vibe is perfect.
Let me enjoy it for a minute.

52
00:05:16,520 --> 00:05:17,400
Koh.

53
00:05:18,520 --> 00:05:22,320
Are you sure I should go
with Sis Hong's group?

54
00:05:22,400 --> 00:05:25,320
Yeah, I can take care of myself.

55
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:29,040
Those guys are still young.
I'll feel better if you go with them.

56
00:05:48,120 --> 00:05:51,200
Are you sure you can find the place?

57
00:05:51,280 --> 00:05:53,240
The other building is 15 kilometers away.

58
00:05:53,320 --> 00:05:54,200
Don't worry.

59
00:05:54,280 --> 00:05:56,800
Technology is amazing these days.

60
00:05:56,880 --> 00:05:58,760
Look.

61
00:05:59,360 --> 00:06:01,720
We've got a signal.

62
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:04,520
Then shall we head out, Captain?

63
00:06:06,120 --> 00:06:07,160
Yes!

64
00:06:07,680 --> 00:06:08,920
-Get in the car.
-Koh.

65
00:06:09,520 --> 00:06:10,880
Let's go.

66
00:06:10,960 --> 00:06:13,160
Whether you find Risa or not,
let me know right away.

67
00:06:13,240 --> 00:06:15,160
-Come on.
-Help me.

68
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:21,120
Be careful.

69
00:06:23,120 --> 00:06:24,320
Hey, get down.

70
00:06:24,960 --> 00:06:25,760
Alright.

71
00:06:27,520 --> 00:06:29,080
Hurry up. Don't let them spot us.

72
00:06:29,760 --> 00:06:31,600
-Let's go.
-Hey, help me.

73
00:06:31,680 --> 00:06:33,240
Come on up.

74
00:06:33,320 --> 00:06:35,360
-You okay?
-Yeah.

75
00:06:50,200 --> 00:06:51,240
Your name is Oab, right?

76
00:06:53,400 --> 00:06:54,680
I'm Risa.

77
00:06:56,760 --> 00:06:58,080
Thanks for helping me.

78
00:06:58,880 --> 00:07:03,000
If I'd gotten caught, they would've locked
me in the basement again for a week.

79
00:07:05,320 --> 00:07:06,320
The basement?

80
00:07:07,680 --> 00:07:12,000
They drag people down there
when they do something seriously wrong.

81
00:07:12,080 --> 00:07:15,040
Some people stay there for months.

82
00:07:15,120 --> 00:07:18,160
Sometimes, well-dressed men
come down there too.

83
00:07:20,360 --> 00:07:22,600
<i>The last thing I heard about Aek</i>

84
00:07:23,200 --> 00:07:25,160
was that Mr. Louis captured him.

85
00:07:25,240 --> 00:07:28,600
Honestly, I don't know
what Aek did to him,

86
00:07:28,680 --> 00:07:30,640
but it must've been serious.

87
00:07:32,840 --> 00:07:35,400
Those well-dressed men…
Was one of them named Louis?

88
00:07:37,400 --> 00:07:38,240
Yes.

89
00:07:40,840 --> 00:07:42,760
I overheard the guards saying

90
00:07:42,840 --> 00:07:44,280
he owns this place.

91
00:07:49,040 --> 00:07:50,240
Why are you asking?

92
00:07:56,760 --> 00:08:00,800
I took this job
because I'm looking for someone.

93
00:08:02,240 --> 00:08:05,800
I heard Louis was the one
who brought him here.

94
00:08:07,880 --> 00:08:10,840
Oab, when you were locked up,

95
00:08:11,880 --> 00:08:13,680
was there anyone else down there?

96
00:08:19,800 --> 00:08:22,240
I don't know what you're planning,

97
00:08:22,760 --> 00:08:24,880
but you shouldn't go down there.

98
00:08:30,400 --> 00:08:32,080
The water's barely running,

99
00:08:32,159 --> 00:08:33,520
and it's so hot.

100
00:08:55,840 --> 00:08:57,200
Wait.

101
00:08:57,280 --> 00:09:01,040
Can you slow down a bit?
I'm getting carsick.

102
00:09:01,120 --> 00:09:02,480
Sorry, sis.

103
00:09:02,560 --> 00:09:03,880
Hang in there for Risa.

104
00:09:06,440 --> 00:09:09,640
Hey, not standing anymore?
Weren't you Tomb Raider a minute ago?

105
00:09:09,720 --> 00:09:10,960
I can't do this anymore!

106
00:09:33,160 --> 00:09:34,560
Hey, wait.

107
00:09:35,200 --> 00:09:36,240
They're with us.

108
00:09:37,320 --> 00:09:38,160
Hey.

109
00:09:39,320 --> 00:09:40,880
They'll take us inside.

110
00:09:41,840 --> 00:09:42,840
Put the gun away.

111
00:09:50,600 --> 00:09:51,880
Let's go, Captain.

112
00:09:52,520 --> 00:09:53,400
Hey.

113
00:11:08,080 --> 00:11:11,560
Don't worry. Like I said,
I've already cleared everything.

114
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:42,080
Koh.

115
00:12:13,760 --> 00:12:15,960
If you go down there,
you'll definitely get caught.

116
00:12:16,560 --> 00:12:18,320
There are guards everywhere downstairs.

117
00:12:28,040 --> 00:12:29,480
Pao, how many kilometers left?

118
00:12:31,040 --> 00:12:34,120
Just keep going straight.
We're less than a kilometer away.

119
00:12:34,200 --> 00:12:37,080
Wow, this signal booster is amazing.

120
00:12:37,160 --> 00:12:39,120
The connection is crystal clear.
Look, sis.

121
00:12:39,880 --> 00:12:41,120
Just focus on driving.

122
00:12:48,360 --> 00:12:50,760
The person you're looking for
is in the room inside.

123
00:12:52,080 --> 00:12:54,680
-Hey, Risa's in there?
-Yeah.

124
00:13:18,720 --> 00:13:20,800
Took you long enough, Koh.

125
00:13:22,600 --> 00:13:24,280
I've been waiting for you.

126
00:13:30,240 --> 00:13:31,600
You betrayed me?

127
00:13:37,440 --> 00:13:38,880
Run, you guys! It's a trap!

128
00:13:38,960 --> 00:13:40,160
Huh?

129
00:13:41,840 --> 00:13:44,840
What did you say? Koh!

130
00:13:47,600 --> 00:13:49,240
Koh, can you hear me?

131
00:13:49,320 --> 00:13:50,600
What did Koh say?

132
00:13:51,560 --> 00:13:52,520
He told us to run.

133
00:13:52,600 --> 00:13:53,440
Hey.

134
00:13:55,320 --> 00:13:57,560
I think he's been betrayed.

135
00:14:07,800 --> 00:14:09,640
Good job, Au.

136
00:14:09,720 --> 00:14:12,160
Always at your service, sir.

137
00:14:14,840 --> 00:14:17,720
What should we do about the group
heading to the other building?

138
00:14:28,400 --> 00:14:29,720
Pao, look at this.

139
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:34,680
Hello? Koh!

140
00:14:35,600 --> 00:14:38,280
Can you hear me? Koh!

141
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:46,920
Chen! They'll hear us and come after us.

142
00:15:03,600 --> 00:15:04,680
They're watching us.

143
00:15:05,280 --> 00:15:06,880
-What did you say?
-Hey, sis!

144
00:15:07,600 --> 00:15:09,600
Keep it down, sis. They'll hear us.

145
00:15:15,600 --> 00:15:17,200
Okay.

146
00:15:20,200 --> 00:15:21,400
-Chen.
-Huh?

147
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:23,600
I think we should get out of here.

148
00:15:23,680 --> 00:15:25,320
We can figure everything else out later.

149
00:15:30,800 --> 00:15:31,960
Hold on tight.

150
00:15:34,960 --> 00:15:36,800
Hey, they've spotted us! Fire!

151
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:40,320
Hurry up!

152
00:15:42,920 --> 00:15:44,240
Hey, let's go!

153
00:15:53,440 --> 00:15:55,360
I told you not to go down there, didn't I?

154
00:15:57,320 --> 00:15:59,720
The person I'm looking for is my dad.

155
00:16:01,760 --> 00:16:05,840
I think he might be locked up there

156
00:16:05,920 --> 00:16:07,480
in the basement.

157
00:16:07,560 --> 00:16:10,960
No way. I've been
locked down there a few times.

158
00:16:11,040 --> 00:16:13,600
From what I've seen, they only keep
people there who tried to escape.

159
00:16:13,680 --> 00:16:16,720
They don't hold outsiders
who don't work here.

160
00:16:18,520 --> 00:16:20,480
But I just saw

161
00:16:21,200 --> 00:16:22,920
my friend go down there.

162
00:16:23,840 --> 00:16:25,440
If no one's being held there,

163
00:16:26,720 --> 00:16:28,320
why would he go down?

164
00:16:28,920 --> 00:16:32,400
Risa, the last time
I was taken down there,

165
00:16:32,480 --> 00:16:34,800
there wasn't anyone being held at all.

166
00:16:55,080 --> 00:16:57,040
It's okay now.

167
00:17:00,520 --> 00:17:01,400
I can't wait any longer.

168
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:03,920
Wait. Where are you going?

169
00:17:04,640 --> 00:17:05,520
To save Koh.

170
00:17:05,599 --> 00:17:07,319
Calm down. Pull yourself together.

171
00:17:07,400 --> 00:17:09,400
What are we waiting for?
For my friend to die?

172
00:17:09,480 --> 00:17:10,720
Risa is my friend too!

173
00:17:12,520 --> 00:17:14,800
If we rush in there without a plan,

174
00:17:14,880 --> 00:17:16,400
both of them will die for sure.

175
00:17:17,440 --> 00:17:20,520
He's right. They ambushed us this badly.

176
00:17:20,599 --> 00:17:22,960
If we charge in blindly,
it's a suicide mission.

177
00:17:23,560 --> 00:17:26,280
Let's wait and see
what they want to negotiate.

178
00:17:31,480 --> 00:17:33,560
Who the hell is calling now?

179
00:17:34,880 --> 00:17:35,960
Hello. Who is this?

180
00:17:36,560 --> 00:17:38,080
Angpao, it's me.

181
00:17:39,920 --> 00:17:40,760
Ris!

182
00:17:41,560 --> 00:17:43,520
-Where are you, Ris?
-Pao!

183
00:17:43,600 --> 00:17:46,040
Ris, are you okay?

184
00:17:46,120 --> 00:17:48,160
-Mungkorn?
<i>-Ris.</i>

185
00:17:48,240 --> 00:17:50,240
We know you came to Poipet
looking for your dad.

186
00:17:51,160 --> 00:17:52,760
<i>You're at the call center compound,</i>
<i>aren't you?</i>

187
00:17:52,840 --> 00:17:56,120
Did you come with Koh?

188
00:17:57,400 --> 00:17:59,080
Yeah. How did you know?

189
00:17:59,160 --> 00:18:02,440
I saw him go into the building
where I work.

190
00:18:05,200 --> 00:18:07,920
Okay, Ris. Listen carefully.

191
00:18:08,640 --> 00:18:10,440
Koh's been captured.

192
00:18:11,040 --> 00:18:13,200
<i>Don't do anything reckless.</i>

193
00:18:13,280 --> 00:18:16,560
We're figuring out
a way to get inside. Okay?

194
00:18:22,160 --> 00:18:26,520
Mung, how are we supposed
to get into that building?

195
00:19:04,080 --> 00:19:06,080
Long sleep, Koh.

196
00:19:08,040 --> 00:19:08,960
James!

197
00:19:09,040 --> 00:19:11,640
You really are as stupid
as a servant's son.

198
00:19:12,320 --> 00:19:15,640
Did you really think Aek was here?

199
00:19:18,320 --> 00:19:21,200
And that group who escaped last night…

200
00:19:21,840 --> 00:19:23,280
That's the Admin gang, isn't it?

201
00:19:36,160 --> 00:19:39,440
Don't worry. You won't be lonely for long.

202
00:19:39,520 --> 00:19:42,920
I'm going to capture all your friends
and lock them up right here with you.

203
00:19:49,840 --> 00:19:51,400
And that friend of yours
who's already here…

204
00:19:54,200 --> 00:19:55,600
I'm going to get her too.

205
00:20:00,720 --> 00:20:01,680
Move.

206
00:20:08,480 --> 00:20:11,360
These two have been here the longest.

207
00:20:12,760 --> 00:20:15,960
Don't worry. I'm not going to hurt you.

208
00:20:16,600 --> 00:20:18,920
I just need you two

209
00:20:19,520 --> 00:20:21,400
to help me find someone.

210
00:20:28,520 --> 00:20:30,360
New arrivals, listen up.

211
00:20:30,440 --> 00:20:32,760
Take out your phones and turn them off.

212
00:20:32,840 --> 00:20:34,240
The guards will collect them.

213
00:20:34,960 --> 00:20:37,280
The only thing you're allowed
to bring inside

214
00:20:37,360 --> 00:20:39,040
are your clothes and personal belongings.

215
00:20:39,120 --> 00:20:42,360
If anyone is caught hiding a phone,

216
00:20:42,440 --> 00:20:45,320
you will be severely punished.

217
00:21:01,680 --> 00:21:04,760
Risa, the guards just called me in.

218
00:21:04,840 --> 00:21:07,120
I think they're looking for you.

219
00:21:32,160 --> 00:21:35,200
This is the cafeteria. Eat quickly.

220
00:21:35,280 --> 00:21:37,000
You'll have to start work right away.

221
00:22:01,880 --> 00:22:03,720
Pao, I've found Ris.

222
00:22:03,800 --> 00:22:05,680
Hey! We've found Ris!

223
00:22:06,640 --> 00:22:09,640
I'll talk to her and figure out a way out.
I'll contact you later.

224
00:22:09,720 --> 00:22:11,920
Got it. I'll keep a low profile for now.

225
00:22:12,000 --> 00:22:13,840
Let's go, Chen.

226
00:22:20,280 --> 00:22:22,200
MEET ME BY THE RESTROOM IN FIVE MINUTES

227
00:22:38,960 --> 00:22:40,960
Wait, where are you going?

228
00:22:41,840 --> 00:22:42,920
I'll be right back.

229
00:23:29,480 --> 00:23:31,560
Risa, are you okay?

230
00:23:31,640 --> 00:23:33,640
Mung, I'm okay.

231
00:23:34,640 --> 00:23:37,200
They already know
someone infiltrated this place,

232
00:23:37,280 --> 00:23:40,640
but they still don't know it's you.
I'll figure something out.

233
00:23:40,720 --> 00:23:43,000
Tonight, I'll get you out of here.

234
00:23:43,080 --> 00:23:43,960
What about Koh?

235
00:23:44,040 --> 00:23:46,680
I saw him come in and get taken
down to the basement last night.

236
00:23:46,760 --> 00:23:48,360
He still hasn't come back up.

237
00:23:49,800 --> 00:23:54,000
He was working with someone inside
to help you,

238
00:23:54,080 --> 00:23:55,600
but I think he's been betrayed.

239
00:23:55,680 --> 00:23:58,320
Then what are we going to do?

240
00:23:58,400 --> 00:24:02,160
I don't know yet.
I have to get you out first.

241
00:24:02,240 --> 00:24:05,000
We'll deal with Koh afterward.

242
00:24:07,840 --> 00:24:09,200
The power only went out on this floor.

243
00:24:09,280 --> 00:24:11,040
Find out where the short circuit is.

244
00:24:12,680 --> 00:24:15,560
We'll update each other during
the dinner break. Let's split up for now.

245
00:24:38,160 --> 00:24:39,600
Where did you go?

246
00:24:40,480 --> 00:24:43,600
The new guy is my friend.
He came here to help me escape.

247
00:24:44,720 --> 00:24:49,040
In all the time I've been here,
no one has ever escaped.

248
00:24:49,120 --> 00:24:51,920
And now, they're already looking for you.

249
00:24:52,000 --> 00:24:54,040
It's too dangerous.

250
00:24:55,200 --> 00:24:58,160
My dad isn't here.
There's no reason for me to stay anymore.

251
00:25:00,960 --> 00:25:03,000
Oab, will you come with me?

252
00:25:04,400 --> 00:25:08,080
I know you want to get out of here.
You want to go back to your dad.

253
00:25:09,080 --> 00:25:09,960
Come with me.

254
00:25:16,720 --> 00:25:18,960
That girl's name is Risa.

255
00:25:19,040 --> 00:25:22,760
She joined three days ago.
The guy who came to help her

256
00:25:22,840 --> 00:25:25,280
arrived this morning
with the new recruits.

257
00:25:26,280 --> 00:25:28,520
The new recruits?

258
00:25:33,160 --> 00:25:34,160
Found him.

259
00:25:49,960 --> 00:25:50,800
Zoom in on him.

260
00:25:59,600 --> 00:26:01,080
CIVIL REGISTRATION CERTIFICATE

261
00:26:04,840 --> 00:26:07,120
We've got another one
walking right into the trap.

262
00:26:08,320 --> 00:26:09,200
Go get him.

263
00:26:09,280 --> 00:26:10,200
Yes, sir.

264
00:26:25,320 --> 00:26:28,200
Hey, find these two immediately.

265
00:26:28,280 --> 00:26:29,320
Which ones?

266
00:26:30,200 --> 00:26:32,640
They just sent over their photos. The guy

267
00:26:32,720 --> 00:26:35,640
just arrived, and the girl's name is Risa.

268
00:26:35,720 --> 00:26:37,640
She hasn't been here long either.

269
00:26:38,480 --> 00:26:41,640
Hello. Is this Mr. Jamrat Thongrung?

270
00:26:41,720 --> 00:26:44,880
This is the Metropolitan Police Bureau.

271
00:26:44,960 --> 00:26:48,560
We're calling to inform you
that you have an outstanding traffic fine

272
00:26:48,640 --> 00:26:50,120
that is now subject to enforcement…

273
00:26:50,200 --> 00:26:53,720
I think I recognize her.
She's on Team Three under Miang.

274
00:26:53,800 --> 00:26:55,960
Good. Call him right now.

275
00:26:56,480 --> 00:26:57,360
Got it.

276
00:27:02,680 --> 00:27:04,360
Hello, yes.

277
00:27:04,440 --> 00:27:06,080
Guard Miang speaking.

278
00:27:16,280 --> 00:27:17,920
No problem at all.

279
00:27:18,000 --> 00:27:20,480
Miang, why weren't you
answering your phone?

280
00:27:20,560 --> 00:27:21,800
I was on another call.

281
00:27:21,880 --> 00:27:23,280
Isn't this girl on your team?

282
00:27:26,200 --> 00:27:27,800
Yes, she is.

283
00:27:31,240 --> 00:27:34,240
-Where did she go?
-To the restroom. What's going on?

284
00:27:39,400 --> 00:27:40,400
I think I recognize her.

285
00:27:40,480 --> 00:27:42,840
-She's on Team Three under Miang.
-Good.

286
00:27:42,920 --> 00:27:44,280
Call him right now.

287
00:27:44,960 --> 00:27:46,040
-Let's go.
-Got it.

288
00:28:01,480 --> 00:28:03,680
Sorry, I walked into the wrong room.

289
00:28:05,520 --> 00:28:07,880
Oh, it's you.

290
00:28:08,800 --> 00:28:11,880
Our beautiful Miss Nao.
What can I do for you?

291
00:28:12,880 --> 00:28:15,440
Excuse me. May I use the restroom?

292
00:28:18,120 --> 00:28:20,480
Wow, it's Miss Nao.

293
00:28:21,520 --> 00:28:22,360
What's going on?

294
00:28:23,000 --> 00:28:24,840
I'm always at your service.

295
00:28:26,920 --> 00:28:29,080
What? You're getting out now?

296
00:28:29,160 --> 00:28:30,880
Yeah, they're starting to catch on.

297
00:28:30,960 --> 00:28:34,800
Turn back and wait behind the building.
Ris and I will come out through the back.

298
00:28:34,880 --> 00:28:35,720
Got it.

299
00:28:35,800 --> 00:28:37,800
-Hey, what's going on?
-What's up?

300
00:28:37,880 --> 00:28:40,640
Change of plans, sis.
Mung is bringing Ris out right now.

301
00:28:40,720 --> 00:28:41,800
Right now?

302
00:28:41,880 --> 00:28:44,960
You can't do that. It's broad daylight.
Trying to get out now is way too risky.

303
00:28:45,040 --> 00:28:47,920
I don't know anymore. Just hurry.

304
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:50,120
Chen, take the back route now.

305
00:28:50,200 --> 00:28:52,680
-Hey, but--
-Just go! Trust me.

306
00:28:52,760 --> 00:28:53,800
Ris, let's go.

307
00:28:53,880 --> 00:28:55,720
Hey, wait. We have to help Koh.

308
00:28:55,800 --> 00:28:59,160
No. We need to get out first,
then we'll come back for him.

309
00:28:59,240 --> 00:29:01,080
-But…
-Listen, Ris.

310
00:29:01,160 --> 00:29:03,720
If we get caught, everyone dies.

311
00:29:06,560 --> 00:29:07,960
You didn't find them?

312
00:29:09,160 --> 00:29:12,960
Then go find them. Don't let them escape.

313
00:29:13,480 --> 00:29:15,160
-Move!
-Yes, sir.

314
00:29:26,360 --> 00:29:28,920
Hey, hold on. You check the back.
I'll cover the other side.

315
00:29:29,000 --> 00:29:30,400
-Yeah, got it.
-Go.

316
00:29:34,080 --> 00:29:34,960
Now.

317
00:29:37,840 --> 00:29:39,840
Oab, You scared me.

318
00:29:39,920 --> 00:29:42,680
If you're planning to use the back exit,
you're making a mistake.

319
00:29:42,760 --> 00:29:45,240
Don't worry. We've got people
outside helping us.

320
00:29:45,320 --> 00:29:47,320
Trust me, they have even more people.

321
00:29:47,400 --> 00:29:49,680
They've probably already called
reinforcements to block every exit.

322
00:29:50,920 --> 00:29:52,480
Like I told you,

323
00:29:52,560 --> 00:29:56,320
no one has ever escaped from here.

324
00:30:03,720 --> 00:30:05,080
There are way too many of them.

325
00:30:06,160 --> 00:30:07,280
How are they supposed to get out?

326
00:30:11,800 --> 00:30:13,400
Hey, Angpao.

327
00:30:13,480 --> 00:30:16,520
Can you tell Mungkorn to wait until
tonight? It'll be safer to escape then.

328
00:30:16,600 --> 00:30:20,360
No, Chen. If we wait that long,
my friends won't make it.

329
00:30:20,880 --> 00:30:21,960
But…

330
00:30:22,560 --> 00:30:23,840
if you're willing to risk it,

331
00:30:23,920 --> 00:30:27,840
you'd be better off using the side gate
connected to the abandoned warehouse.

332
00:30:27,920 --> 00:30:29,720
It's secured with a chain.

333
00:30:29,800 --> 00:30:32,880
Tell the people outside to cut it,
and they can open the gate.

334
00:30:35,800 --> 00:30:37,960
Pao, can you hear me?

335
00:30:38,680 --> 00:30:41,040
-What's up?
-Do you have bolt cutters in the car?

336
00:30:48,520 --> 00:30:51,000
Yes, I told you I came fully prepared.

337
00:30:51,080 --> 00:30:54,920
Good. Go wait at the side gate
by the abandoned warehouse.

338
00:30:55,000 --> 00:30:58,680
Cut the chain at the gate.
We'll use that exit instead.

339
00:30:59,520 --> 00:31:00,880
Then good luck, Risa.

340
00:31:01,520 --> 00:31:03,640
Oab, aren't you coming with me?

341
00:31:03,720 --> 00:31:07,320
I can't go yet. You guys go. I'll be fine.

342
00:31:07,920 --> 00:31:11,360
Why? Don't you want to see your dad?

343
00:31:13,200 --> 00:31:15,880
He's the reason I ended up here.

344
00:31:22,600 --> 00:31:24,760
Alright. See you there.

345
00:31:26,560 --> 00:31:28,000
Ris, let's go.

346
00:32:02,320 --> 00:32:04,640
Stop. Stop the car.

347
00:32:04,720 --> 00:32:06,040
Kill the engine.

348
00:32:16,240 --> 00:32:18,400
There's really no one here.

349
00:32:19,000 --> 00:32:19,920
Hurry.

350
00:32:20,440 --> 00:32:23,040
<i>Mung, I'm at the side gate.</i>

351
00:32:23,120 --> 00:32:25,440
Okay. Cut the chain. We're almost there.

352
00:32:26,840 --> 00:32:27,680
Let's go, sis.

353
00:32:30,800 --> 00:32:31,760
Go.

354
00:32:33,640 --> 00:32:34,600
We're here.

355
00:32:37,560 --> 00:32:39,040
Cut this chain.

356
00:32:50,480 --> 00:32:51,680
Done.

357
00:32:51,760 --> 00:32:53,080
-That was easy.
-Nice work.

358
00:32:53,160 --> 00:32:55,400
Be careful, okay?

359
00:33:29,520 --> 00:33:31,600
Angpao, run!

360
00:33:32,160 --> 00:33:33,280
Don't shoot!

361
00:33:39,000 --> 00:33:40,200
Angpao!

362
00:33:41,720 --> 00:33:43,360
Run!

363
00:33:45,600 --> 00:33:47,120
Run!

364
00:33:52,920 --> 00:33:53,720
Go!

365
00:33:54,480 --> 00:33:55,320
Angpao.

366
00:33:59,600 --> 00:34:01,880
Dad, Mom, please help me!

367
00:34:01,960 --> 00:34:03,720
Oh no.

368
00:34:13,120 --> 00:34:15,920
Geez! What's happening?

369
00:34:16,000 --> 00:34:18,480
What am I supposed to do?

370
00:34:24,000 --> 00:34:25,880
There he is! After him!

371
00:34:25,960 --> 00:34:28,199
They're still chasing me!

372
00:34:29,960 --> 00:34:30,880
Help!

373
00:34:32,760 --> 00:34:34,199
Oh my God.

374
00:34:41,040 --> 00:34:43,560
Dad! Mom!

375
00:34:50,840 --> 00:34:53,280
Spirits of the forest, please save me.

376
00:34:53,360 --> 00:34:54,920
I'm definitely going to die!

377
00:35:53,760 --> 00:35:54,640
Come on!

378
00:36:05,480 --> 00:36:07,160
Uncle!

379
00:36:10,280 --> 00:36:11,360
Uncle!

380
00:36:11,440 --> 00:36:13,640
You guys…

381
00:36:21,040 --> 00:36:22,440
Hey, grenade!

382
00:36:23,320 --> 00:36:27,120
Why are you just sitting there?
Get down! Go!

383
00:36:27,200 --> 00:36:28,920
-Come here, kid.
-Yak, get the kid!

384
00:36:30,360 --> 00:36:32,160
Yak, move!

385
00:36:49,640 --> 00:36:52,880
A fake grenade. Damn it!

386
00:36:59,400 --> 00:37:02,440
Uncle, how did you guys end up helping me?

387
00:37:03,240 --> 00:37:05,600
We ran into Koh.

388
00:37:07,000 --> 00:37:09,280
Wow, acting all tough.

389
00:37:09,360 --> 00:37:10,920
Hello. Are you Thai?

390
00:37:11,000 --> 00:37:12,720
Oh, just here for a little fun.

391
00:37:12,800 --> 00:37:15,160
That was close.

392
00:37:20,960 --> 00:37:22,960
Yak, why aren't you coming?

393
00:37:23,040 --> 00:37:24,200
What are you doing?

394
00:37:25,600 --> 00:37:28,000
-He looks familiar.
-Familiar how?

395
00:37:28,880 --> 00:37:30,160
Nothing. Let's go gamble.

396
00:37:31,480 --> 00:37:32,960
You made me walk
all the way over here for nothing.

397
00:37:38,720 --> 00:37:41,160
-Why are you standing here again?
-Hey, Gao.

398
00:37:41,240 --> 00:37:42,640
-What?
-I think…

399
00:37:42,720 --> 00:37:44,520
I saw Koh.

400
00:37:46,120 --> 00:37:47,000
Koh?

401
00:37:47,080 --> 00:37:48,440
-What?
-Come here.

402
00:37:48,520 --> 00:37:51,440
You're seeing things.
Why would he be here?

403
00:37:51,520 --> 00:37:52,440
Just trust me.

404
00:37:53,200 --> 00:37:54,200
You bastard.

405
00:37:56,080 --> 00:37:57,680
Let's get straight to the point.

406
00:37:57,760 --> 00:37:59,400
Does Louis come here often?

407
00:37:59,480 --> 00:38:00,920
It really is him.

408
00:38:01,800 --> 00:38:05,720
Why the hell is he here?

409
00:38:07,320 --> 00:38:11,040
So what's going on? Tell me everything.

410
00:38:19,880 --> 00:38:22,960
What are we supposed to do now?

411
00:38:23,040 --> 00:38:25,720
Are we just going to sit here
and wait to die?

412
00:38:27,360 --> 00:38:29,960
I'm quiet because I'm thinking.

413
00:38:30,600 --> 00:38:33,920
Actually, it might not be such a bad thing
that we're all locked up together.

414
00:38:34,000 --> 00:38:35,920
More heads are better than one.

415
00:38:36,960 --> 00:38:40,360
Sis, as long as Angpao hasn't been caught,
we still have hope.

416
00:38:40,960 --> 00:38:43,400
He's probably already on his way
back to Thailand by now.

417
00:38:48,120 --> 00:38:50,400
Quiet. Someone's coming.

418
00:38:54,280 --> 00:38:55,240
Wow.

419
00:39:01,000 --> 00:39:02,400
Looks like almost everyone's here.

420
00:39:15,520 --> 00:39:17,360
CIVIL REGISTRATION CERTIFICATE

421
00:39:18,880 --> 00:39:20,360
CIVIL REGISTRATION CERTIFICATE

422
00:39:29,400 --> 00:39:32,320
Now we're only missing two old men

423
00:39:33,200 --> 00:39:34,160
and one fat guy.

424
00:39:35,080 --> 00:39:36,160
Hey.

425
00:39:36,840 --> 00:39:40,560
I've caught more of you
than Louis even asked for.

426
00:39:45,160 --> 00:39:47,000
Where did you take my dad?

427
00:39:49,040 --> 00:39:50,120
Your dad?

428
00:39:53,200 --> 00:39:55,160
-Who is your dad?
-Nothing.

429
00:39:55,680 --> 00:39:57,840
She's talking nonsense.
She thinks her dad got tricked

430
00:39:57,920 --> 00:40:00,480
into working at a call center,
so she followed him here.

431
00:40:01,120 --> 00:40:03,680
My dad's name is Aek.
He used to work with you at Hyena pub.

432
00:40:11,080 --> 00:40:13,720
I've got one more question.
Where's Aek now?

433
00:40:14,680 --> 00:40:17,640
Why are you suddenly
asking about him? Feeling guilty?

434
00:40:18,520 --> 00:40:20,160
Want to apologize to him?

435
00:40:24,640 --> 00:40:28,160
Oh, don't tell me this girl

436
00:40:29,200 --> 00:40:30,880
is Aek's daughter?

437
00:40:31,480 --> 00:40:33,840
If Louis finds out,

438
00:40:33,920 --> 00:40:35,440
he's going to be very surprised.

439
00:40:41,600 --> 00:40:44,200
So everyone's being held
at the call center compound?

440
00:40:48,000 --> 00:40:49,480
Why did you run off on your own?

441
00:40:50,680 --> 00:40:51,960
What would you have done if you were me?

442
00:40:52,640 --> 00:40:53,640
Fight, of course.

443
00:40:54,560 --> 00:40:56,640
Exactly. We're going to fight.

444
00:40:56,720 --> 00:40:59,480
I'm saving my friends,
and you can help save Sis Hong.

445
00:41:01,720 --> 00:41:03,600
Hey, no.

446
00:41:03,680 --> 00:41:06,000
That's not our problem. This is your mess.

447
00:41:06,080 --> 00:41:08,040
Yeah. This is your problem.

448
00:41:08,120 --> 00:41:10,400
We've stayed out of Hong's business
for a long time now.

449
00:41:10,480 --> 00:41:11,560
Why should we help her?

450
00:41:11,640 --> 00:41:13,120
Then why did you help me?

451
00:41:14,160 --> 00:41:16,080
You should've just left me to die.

452
00:41:16,600 --> 00:41:18,760
That would've been better than
dealing with two cold-hearted old men.

453
00:41:18,840 --> 00:41:22,240
Hey, brat! How can you say that?
We helped you. Show some gratitude.

454
00:41:22,320 --> 00:41:25,720
Grab your stuff from the back of the truck
and go wherever you want.

455
00:41:26,840 --> 00:41:29,120
Do you know Sis Hong has cancer?

456
00:41:34,080 --> 00:41:37,080
What cancer? You're lying.

457
00:41:37,160 --> 00:41:37,840
I'm telling the truth.

458
00:41:40,000 --> 00:41:41,360
Why would she lie to me?

459
00:41:41,440 --> 00:41:43,280
Believe it or don't. I don't care.

460
00:41:43,360 --> 00:41:45,480
I'll find a way to go back
and save them myself.

461
00:41:47,840 --> 00:41:49,040
Hold on.

462
00:41:52,320 --> 00:41:54,560
Look at yourself.

463
00:41:54,640 --> 00:41:57,320
Seriously, look at yourself.
If you charge in like that

464
00:41:57,400 --> 00:41:59,880
without a plan,
how do you expect to survive?

465
00:42:02,440 --> 00:42:05,000
Fine. We'll go with you.

466
00:42:05,840 --> 00:42:08,040
But don't get it twisted.
We're not doing it for Hong.

467
00:42:08,720 --> 00:42:10,680
We're only helping you, fat kid.

468
00:42:10,760 --> 00:42:12,880
Whoa, so sensitive.

469
00:42:14,160 --> 00:42:15,400
Such a fragile ego.

470
00:42:15,960 --> 00:42:17,600
Is this what they call old man's pride?

471
00:42:17,680 --> 00:42:19,400
-Yeah. Huh?
-Yeah. Hey!

472
00:42:28,480 --> 00:42:29,320
Go.

473
00:42:29,400 --> 00:42:30,520
Look at that.

474
00:42:32,200 --> 00:42:33,080
A little more.

475
00:42:34,160 --> 00:42:35,680
-Stop.
-Okay.

476
00:42:35,760 --> 00:42:37,080
Perfect.

477
00:42:37,880 --> 00:42:41,080
This is it for you. You're done.

478
00:42:41,160 --> 00:42:42,560
Drop.

479
00:42:43,400 --> 00:42:44,920
I've got you.

480
00:42:45,000 --> 00:42:46,080
We'll see about that.

481
00:42:47,840 --> 00:42:50,040
Hey, you idiot! Yak!

482
00:42:50,120 --> 00:42:52,640
Don't mess this up.
I told you to stop. Are you okay?

483
00:42:52,720 --> 00:42:53,760
I'm fine.

484
00:42:53,840 --> 00:42:55,680
-You sure?
-What's going on?

485
00:42:55,760 --> 00:42:56,760
Damn it.

486
00:42:57,840 --> 00:42:59,720
-I'll go out there.
-Okay.

487
00:43:01,520 --> 00:43:03,000
-You sure you're okay?
-Okay.

488
00:43:14,440 --> 00:43:19,080
Hey, Bo! How did you end up here, Bo?

489
00:43:19,680 --> 00:43:21,440
What Bo? You've got the wrong guy.

490
00:43:22,880 --> 00:43:24,560
I'm Akaradet.

491
00:43:24,640 --> 00:43:25,880
Akaradet?

492
00:43:26,640 --> 00:43:29,320
I don't have a friend named Akaradet.

493
00:43:29,400 --> 00:43:33,240
I'm Akaradet, Ittikorn's brother,
Uthumphon's boyfriend,

494
00:43:33,320 --> 00:43:36,560
from Uthai. Teacher Angkhana
will definitely know me.

495
00:43:37,960 --> 00:43:39,280
You got rich and forgot your friends.

496
00:43:41,320 --> 00:43:42,920
Hey, bro. Let's have a drink together.

497
00:43:43,520 --> 00:43:45,080
Cheers!

498
00:43:47,320 --> 00:43:48,320
What is wrong with these people?

499
00:43:50,560 --> 00:43:51,400
They're weird.

500
00:43:59,000 --> 00:44:00,280
Yes!

501
00:44:02,400 --> 00:44:05,160
Yeah, it's over.

502
00:44:14,480 --> 00:44:15,840
Why did you capture me?

503
00:44:15,920 --> 00:44:17,200
Don't you know who I am?

504
00:44:17,280 --> 00:44:18,440
I know.

505
00:44:19,840 --> 00:44:21,640
You're the one who betrayed us.

506
00:44:23,200 --> 00:44:26,880
And we're here to get revenge for him.

507
00:44:28,520 --> 00:44:30,000
You've been inside
the call center building, right?

508
00:44:34,280 --> 00:44:37,080
Here. Draw us a map.

509
00:44:37,160 --> 00:44:39,680
Show us where Koh is being held.

510
00:44:43,200 --> 00:44:44,400
I'm not drawing anything.

511
00:44:46,840 --> 00:44:48,400
You think I'm scared of you?

512
00:44:49,600 --> 00:44:51,640
Hey, come here.

513
00:44:52,680 --> 00:44:53,400
Yak.

514
00:44:54,440 --> 00:44:55,600
Take care of him.

515
00:45:23,720 --> 00:45:25,760
Oops, sorry! I didn't mean it.

516
00:45:28,240 --> 00:45:32,000
Oh no, your face!
Sorry, I really didn't mean it.

517
00:45:34,480 --> 00:45:38,320
That wasn't even on purpose.
If you don't draw the map,

518
00:45:38,400 --> 00:45:40,680
my friend here is going to stab you

519
00:45:40,760 --> 00:45:42,080
in the back with this knife.

520
00:45:42,160 --> 00:45:44,200
For real. Like this!

521
00:45:45,160 --> 00:45:48,360
Oh no! Sorry!

522
00:45:49,480 --> 00:45:51,320
Stop. That's enough.

523
00:45:51,400 --> 00:45:52,760
Are you going to draw it or not?

524
00:45:52,840 --> 00:45:56,200
Fine, I'll draw it.
Just give me the paper.

525
00:47:11,320 --> 00:47:12,400
Good.

526
00:47:12,480 --> 00:47:14,840
That's it. Drink it.

527
00:47:14,920 --> 00:47:17,880
Good.

528
00:47:36,440 --> 00:47:38,040
There you go.

529
00:47:39,160 --> 00:47:40,360
Piece of cake.

530
00:47:42,280 --> 00:47:43,720
Hold on.

531
00:47:43,800 --> 00:47:45,680
Angpao, the gate is open.

532
00:47:45,760 --> 00:47:47,680
<i>Proceed with the next step.</i>

533
00:47:48,680 --> 00:47:50,200
Copy that.

534
00:48:03,880 --> 00:48:07,320
Come on in, all of you. Let's finish this.

535
00:48:30,800 --> 00:48:32,360
Stop! Don't move!

536
00:48:42,320 --> 00:48:44,000
You're trapped now, idiots.

537
00:48:44,080 --> 00:48:46,560
Slowly, put your guns down. Now!

538
00:48:47,800 --> 00:48:50,800
I said put them down!
Why aren't you lowering your guns?

539
00:48:50,880 --> 00:48:52,240
Do you want to die?

540
00:48:52,320 --> 00:48:56,080
Well, these aren't guns.

541
00:48:57,840 --> 00:48:59,240
They're bananas.

542
00:49:02,880 --> 00:49:03,760
Give me that.

543
00:49:23,920 --> 00:49:25,400
Who the hell are you people?

544
00:49:39,000 --> 00:49:41,160
Hey, you're actually pretty smart.

545
00:49:41,240 --> 00:49:44,560
How did you know they'd set a trap for us?

546
00:49:44,640 --> 00:49:48,120
From the blueprint Uncle Au drew,
there was a CCTV room.

547
00:49:48,640 --> 00:49:51,520
Don't you think
they'd be waiting for us there?

548
00:49:51,600 --> 00:49:53,720
-Impressive.
-You're so smart, boy.

549
00:49:53,800 --> 00:49:55,120
-Hey, don't distract me!
-Yeah.

550
00:50:02,760 --> 00:50:04,640
Uncle, left or right at the end?

551
00:50:04,720 --> 00:50:06,480
-Hey, wait.
-Hurry up.

552
00:50:06,560 --> 00:50:08,360
-Left or right?
-Just a second.

553
00:50:08,440 --> 00:50:09,880
-Quick.
-Right.

554
00:50:09,960 --> 00:50:11,560
-Right.
-Then go straight.

555
00:50:11,640 --> 00:50:14,120
Got it.

556
00:50:18,360 --> 00:50:19,920
Who the hell are you people?

557
00:50:20,840 --> 00:50:24,040
Someone hired us to come here.

558
00:50:24,680 --> 00:50:26,120
You bastard!

559
00:50:28,240 --> 00:50:31,600
Hey! Quick! Get downstairs!
Hurry! To the basement!

560
00:50:42,560 --> 00:50:44,360
Found them. All of them.

561
00:50:45,520 --> 00:50:46,800
What the hell is this?

562
00:50:48,280 --> 00:50:49,840
You found them all, huh?

563
00:50:49,920 --> 00:50:51,680
Then let's do this.

564
00:50:51,760 --> 00:50:55,160
Three, two, one.

565
00:50:57,560 --> 00:50:59,240
INCOMING CALL, BOOM!

566
00:51:06,800 --> 00:51:10,000
INCOMING CALL, BOOM!

567
00:51:10,080 --> 00:51:12,320
Damn it! A bomb!

568
00:51:17,640 --> 00:51:19,880
What's going on up there?

569
00:51:22,520 --> 00:51:23,840
Mission completed.

570
00:51:24,760 --> 00:51:27,480
-Hey, everything okay?
-How'd it go?

571
00:51:27,560 --> 00:51:28,600
Is it done?

572
00:51:30,160 --> 00:51:32,080
How'd it go?

573
00:51:33,080 --> 00:51:36,920
Not sure what happened. The camera just
exploded, and then the feed went dead.

574
00:51:37,000 --> 00:51:37,760
Gao.

575
00:51:38,920 --> 00:51:40,840
It's our turn now.

576
00:51:40,920 --> 00:51:43,840
-Let's go. I'll lead.
-Time to shine.

577
00:51:45,360 --> 00:51:48,480
Hey, what's wrong? You look pale.

578
00:51:50,320 --> 00:51:51,840
I feel kind of weird.

579
00:51:53,080 --> 00:51:54,680
I've never killed anyone before.

580
00:51:55,720 --> 00:52:00,160
It just doesn't feel right. I feel weird.

581
00:52:00,240 --> 00:52:01,760
Those people are bad guys.

582
00:52:01,840 --> 00:52:05,200
They're truly evil. If you hadn't done it,

583
00:52:06,120 --> 00:52:08,280
they would've killed your friends.

584
00:52:10,080 --> 00:52:13,280
Alright. You stay here and keep watch.

585
00:52:14,280 --> 00:52:15,320
If anything happens, call us.

586
00:52:15,400 --> 00:52:17,800
-Yes.
-Alright? Take a deep breath.

587
00:52:21,960 --> 00:52:23,240
-Let's go.
-Let's go.

588
00:52:30,040 --> 00:52:33,120
May all beings who suffer, bound by birth,
aging, sickness, and death,

589
00:52:33,200 --> 00:52:35,120
be free from suffering.

590
00:52:45,920 --> 00:52:48,160
-Bro, is that you?
-Hey, bro!

591
00:52:48,240 --> 00:52:50,240
Gao! Yak!

592
00:52:51,280 --> 00:52:53,280
We're here to get you out.
Are you okay, Ho--

593
00:52:53,360 --> 00:52:54,560
-Yak!
-You guys!

594
00:52:55,320 --> 00:52:56,840
Chen! Koh!

595
00:52:58,520 --> 00:53:01,400
Hey, that explosion earlier,
that was you guys, right?

596
00:53:01,920 --> 00:53:03,040
Yeah.

597
00:53:03,120 --> 00:53:04,920
How did you get in here?
Did you see Angpao?

598
00:53:05,000 --> 00:53:06,280
He's outside keeping watch.

599
00:53:06,360 --> 00:53:09,120
Wait, sorry. Can we talk later?

600
00:53:09,200 --> 00:53:11,480
Or are we going to stand around
until they realize?

601
00:53:11,560 --> 00:53:13,640
-Help us.
-Don't worry.

602
00:53:14,560 --> 00:53:15,280
Yak, hold this.

603
00:53:15,360 --> 00:53:16,200
-Okay.
-Quick.

604
00:53:17,520 --> 00:53:18,720
Easy, bro.

605
00:53:19,320 --> 00:53:23,240
I told you, as long as Angpao
didn't get caught, we still had hope.

606
00:53:24,840 --> 00:53:25,800
Alright.

607
00:53:27,680 --> 00:53:28,640
Yeah.

608
00:53:32,560 --> 00:53:34,360
<i>Angpao, you there?</i>

609
00:53:35,240 --> 00:53:37,960
-What's up, Grandpa?
-Hey, I've got everyone out.

610
00:53:38,040 --> 00:53:39,400
How's it looking outside?

611
00:53:39,480 --> 00:53:41,600
All clear out here. Come on out.

612
00:53:44,160 --> 00:53:45,760
-Follow me.
-Hey, keep it low.

613
00:53:52,280 --> 00:53:53,160
Come on, hurry.

614
00:54:02,520 --> 00:54:03,360
Hong!

615
00:54:03,440 --> 00:54:04,640
-Hong, how bad is it?
-Are you okay?

616
00:54:04,720 --> 00:54:07,080
-It hurts.
-Hong, come on.

617
00:54:07,160 --> 00:54:08,360
-Can you stand?
-I'll help you.

618
00:54:12,600 --> 00:54:14,400
That really hurts.

619
00:54:14,480 --> 00:54:17,800
Hey, we're almost at the exit.
I think it'd be better if we carry her.

620
00:54:17,880 --> 00:54:20,080
Whoever wants to carry her, go ahead.

621
00:54:20,160 --> 00:54:22,640
-I've got bad knees.
-Well.

622
00:54:22,720 --> 00:54:25,000
My L4, L5, and L6
aren't in great shape either.

623
00:54:25,080 --> 00:54:27,760
Bro, are you two really sulking right now?

624
00:54:27,840 --> 00:54:30,240
Can we get out first? You can sulk later.

625
00:54:30,320 --> 00:54:31,800
Who's sulking?

626
00:54:31,880 --> 00:54:34,400
It's okay, I'll carry her.
Sis Hong, I've got you.

627
00:54:34,480 --> 00:54:35,720
-Hurry up.
-We're out of time.

628
00:54:35,800 --> 00:54:37,040
-Quick, go!
-One, two, up!

629
00:54:37,120 --> 00:54:38,440
-Chen.
-Let's go!

630
00:54:38,520 --> 00:54:40,360
-Chen's strong.
-Go!

631
00:54:40,440 --> 00:54:41,840
-Hurry up!
-Go!

632
00:54:51,120 --> 00:54:53,800
You thought I'd die that easily? Dream on!

633
00:54:54,840 --> 00:54:58,120
-Risa!
-Ris!

634
00:54:59,040 --> 00:55:00,120
Get Hong to the car.

635
00:55:00,200 --> 00:55:02,280
We'll handle this.

636
00:55:02,360 --> 00:55:03,520
Then I'm going ahead.

637
00:55:03,600 --> 00:55:05,000
-Go!
-Ris!

638
00:55:10,600 --> 00:55:13,000
The other building's been alerted.
Backup is on the way.

639
00:55:13,800 --> 00:55:14,680
Good.

640
00:55:14,760 --> 00:55:17,360
If we can't take them alive,
kill them all!

641
00:55:21,440 --> 00:55:22,880
Ris, watch out!

642
00:55:22,960 --> 00:55:24,840
-Bro, give it here.
-Hey!

643
00:55:24,920 --> 00:55:25,680
-Hey, kid!
-Don't!

644
00:55:25,760 --> 00:55:26,800
Don't go out there!

645
00:55:27,680 --> 00:55:28,640
Be careful!

646
00:55:29,640 --> 00:55:31,640
Hey, Mung!

647
00:55:31,720 --> 00:55:32,600
Pull him back!

648
00:55:32,680 --> 00:55:34,120
-Come here.
-Drag him back!

649
00:55:36,680 --> 00:55:39,360
Are you trying to get yourself killed?
Give me that gun!

650
00:55:47,920 --> 00:55:50,400
Get out now! More backup is coming!

651
00:55:50,480 --> 00:55:52,040
-Those are fake grenades.
-Who said they're fake?

652
00:55:52,120 --> 00:55:54,080
This time, they're real.

653
00:55:57,920 --> 00:55:58,880
The bullet's still inside.

654
00:55:58,960 --> 00:56:01,440
We can't remove it here.
Let's go to a hospital.

655
00:56:01,520 --> 00:56:02,960
I'm not letting my friends die here!

656
00:56:03,040 --> 00:56:04,000
Mung!

657
00:56:04,800 --> 00:56:06,480
I think my foot's stuck.

658
00:56:06,560 --> 00:56:08,400
You guys should go.
I'll take care of myself.

659
00:56:08,480 --> 00:56:10,840
No. I'm not leaving you behind.

660
00:56:10,920 --> 00:56:13,240
<i>-They have to be around here somewhere.</i>
<i>-They'll keep searching.</i>

661
00:56:13,320 --> 00:56:14,760
<i>Find a place to hide.</i>

662
00:56:14,840 --> 00:56:15,880
<i>Get down. Now!</i>

663
00:56:15,960 --> 00:56:17,960
Just let me do what I want.

664
00:56:18,040 --> 00:56:21,520
<i>I just want to enjoy my life with you guys</i>
<i>one last time before I die.</i>

665
00:56:22,960 --> 00:56:24,480
<i>That's all.</i>

666
00:57:13,400 --> 00:57:15,400
Subtitle translation by:
Chomchanach Yanaharn
